From 2b01931d59436f62880a88e36e90a2c74da1c2a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 23:05:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Performance: faster sinc interpolation, smoother menus

- Sinc interpolation moves its 16-value history with two NEON vext
  instructions per channel instead of up to 15 halfword loads/stores per
  position (shiftInterpolationBuffer). Same buffer contents, verified
  against the old loop on Cortex-A9 code for every shift distance. This
  is most of the per-sample cost of every resampled sample voice that
  isn't playing from a cache (transposed samples, master tune != 440 Hz,
  pitch modulation, first hits, time stretching).
- UI tasks get short maximum intervals (PIC flush, OLED routine, UI timer
  routine, pending UI rendering), so menu changes reach the display
  quickly while audio is busy. The audio routine keeps its priority.
- The sound editor gets every select-encoder detent turned since the last
  time, up to 5 (what its menus already get with shift held), so turns made
  while the card routine held actioning back are not lost.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
